1) Don&#39;t use native javascript. Use a library like jQuery to do ajax.<div><br></div><div>2) Have a look at this video: <a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fB_7_RZgasg" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.youtube.com/watch?v%3DfB_7_RZgasg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793239683703000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3DSenIqN9tzu7bwWSnlYGF">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fB_7_RZgasg</a></div>

<div><br></div><div>3) Perl? Seriously?</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br><div><br></div><div><div class="gmail_quote">On Sun, Aug 5, 2012 at 11:18 PM, michael <span dir="ltr">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">michael...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>

<blockquote class="gmail_quote" style="margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex">Hello,<br><br>I&#39;m wondering if anyone can share an example using Rapache to replace the function of a Perl script in an existing AJAX based web program. In my program, for example, I&#39;d like to replace &quot;<a href="http://perlscript.pl" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://perlscript.pl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793239683703000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1BVnN1iv0Ncd9w4JwQ_z6-">perlscript.pl</a>&quot; with some &quot;Rscript.R&quot; as in the following: <br>

<br>function xmlhttpPost(responsestr) {
<br>  var xmlHttpReq;
<br>  xmlHttpReq = new XMLHttpRequest();                  
<br>  xmlHttpReq.open(&#39;POST&#39;, &quot;<a href="http://localhost/cgi-bin/perlscript.pl" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://localhost/cgi-bin/perlscript.pl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793239683703000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3PqH3pCgqsqnkHvILo7Xky">http://localhost/cgi-bin/perlscript.pl</a>&quot;, true);     
<br>  xmlHttpReq.setRequestHeader(&#39;Content-Type&#39;, &#39;application/x-www-form-urlencoded&#39;);   
<br>  xmlHttpReq.send(responsestr);
<br>  xmlHttpReq.onreadystatechange = function() {   
<br>    if (xmlHttpReq.readyState == 4) {
<br>      var=(xmlHttpReq.responseText);
<br>    }
<br>  }
<br>};<br><br>brew isn&#39;t a good option in this case since the rest of my program (which is pretty large) is already developed. I&#39;d love to see an example showing what the JavaScript, apache config, and R files should all look like. My grasp of the concepts described in the documentation is still pretty weak.<br>

<br>Thanks,<br><br>Michael<span><font color="#888888"><br><br><br><br>

